# Lane policy_audit: were any rules of the routed reading path chosen on benchmark items? (integrity audit; read-only)

## Why
The project reports routed reads on official benchmarks: questions of some types are answered by measurement programs over predicted masks, boxes and geometry. One such result is already recorded: f17 with absolute distance and room size routed scores 65.14 (strict) or 65.4 (with fallback) on official VSI-Bench against 63.79 direct (\`$R/official_reads/ROUTED_ABSDIST_ROOM_VSI5130_20261113.md\`, \`OFFICIAL_RESULTS.md\`, \`FUSION_POLICY_FROZEN_VSI_20261111.md\`, \`FUSION_PROPOSAL_SETTING_FROZEN_VSI_20261113.md\`, \`VSTI_ROUTE_RULE_FROZEN_20261111.md\`). A scene-evidence pass (\`$R/scene_evidence/out/SCENE_EVIDENCE.md\`, record \`EVIDENCE_box_policy*.json\`) reports, without recomputing it, that the box policy \`voteb5_best1\` was chosen on VSI-Bench ScanNet and VSTI items (it cites a record named GT_CEILING_DECOMPOSITION), and that the deployed mask selector was fitted on rooms that include all 44 VSTI rooms and 18 ReVSI rooms. A rule chosen by looking at benchmark items biases the benchmark number it then produces. I need to know exactly which choices in the routed path were made on which data, and how large the bias could be.

